(D6 — a format string as the MATCH of a `treating` clause never fires
 over a list whose elements are all text, though it renders to the
 element: the first line prints kiwi where the manual's reading gives
 matched. The same match fires over a mixed list (third line), and a
 text variable holding the same value fires over the text list (second
 line).
 Ran: /usr/bin/vox D6.vox -o p && ./p   (vox 0.4.16, VOX_CORE_PATH unset)
 expected output:
   kiwi
   matched
   matched
   3
)
a text called word is "kiwi".
print each name from ["kiwi"] treating "{word}" as "matched".
print each name from ["kiwi"] treating word as "matched".
print each name from ["kiwi", 3] treating "{word}" as "matched".
